  "description": "Mobile lifecycle for Shiny.Net.HttpServer, built on Shiny.Core — stops the server when the app is backgrounded and starts it again on resume, keeps it alive on Android through a foreground service, rebinds when the device changes network, and reports the manifest or bundle entries that otherwise fail silently. For iOS and Android, with or without MAUI.",
